+## Hook lifecycle on error
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `onError` and `afterSession` both fire, so a deployer can clean up resources (a span, a handle) that `beforeSession` allocated before it failed ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession-error.acceptance.test.ts#L33)). `afterSession` can assume the session exists but that no user input has been processed and no model response attempted.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
